# City sweep steep-lot-corner (found after city phase 8, fixed in the sim in physics phase 19):
# random keys on a 58-degree lot below Upper Market slide the skater into a building's outside corner,
# where it stopped, wedged, for good (the sweep's 'trapped'). Stopped for half a second on a slope
# steeper than safe ground (ground.safeNormalZ, about 37 degrees) is now wedged: back on the last
# safe spot, stood up (unstuck). City phase 9 then eased the lots themselves (under about 40 degrees;
# this corner is 32 now), so the same keys never wedge at all: no unstuck, still riding at the end.
# The ground wedge rule itself is covered by a lab scenario. Since city phase 11 moved the curbs once,
# the same keys carry on 2 m further and, at tick 940, run head-on at 5 m/s into a building's inside
# corner on a gentle part of the lot, where the skater stops and cannot turn out (no wedge: the
# ground is safe); that is scenarios/city-sweep/building-inside-corner.skate, open.
# Here the run ends just before it (tick 760: since the feel pass's park carve the keys reach the corner
# at about 790; at 910 since physics phase 27).
park sf
cmd 0 traffic clear
cmd 0 teleport -1315 -565 100.56 223
hold up+right 0..72
hold up+flip 72..114
hold up+flip 114..212
hold up+left 212..234
hold up+left 234..294
hold up+right+grab+slide 294..388
hold up+flip+grind 388..502
hold up 502..601
hold up+flip 601..691
hold up 691..750
hold up 750..771
hold left 771..801
hold up+right+grab 801..838
hold up 838..926
hold up+grind 926..971
run 760
expect no event unstuck
expect skater.speed > 1.5 at 760
